# the layer contract: how a chunk's cells are stored, one source for the host
# and the SPIR-V stages
#
# a chunk's storage is a set of layers. a layer holds one value per cell at
# its width, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 or 32 bits. everything that reads or writes cells,
# the CPU's step, the GPU's stages, the census, the draw, the undo journal,
# snapshots, the quadtree's conversions and the file formats, does it through
# this contract: the addressing below in the stages and the pool, and the
# host's planes and sets in cellar.layer.plane. nothing else knows how wide a
# cell is, and only the rule family that declared a layer knows what its
# values mean.
#
# a layer has an owner and a role:
#
#   state  the first layer of every set, declared by the rule family at the
#          width its states need. shared code reads a cell by it, through the
#          family's sense (cellar.layout.Sense): the census, the halo, the
#          pyramids and the draw
#   rule   a further layer the family's step needs, such as a second field,
#          declared by the family with a name and a width. a rule's own data
#          may declare one, as a rule table read from a file would, since a
#          set is data and not code: a layer added changes no layout
#   view   a layer the view keeps for a colour mode, trails, heat or age,
#          declared by a family whose state layer is too narrow to hold its
#          display channels (cellar.rule viewed). it exists only while the
#          view's colour mode uses it (cellar.sim set_views): made from the
#          state as it stands when the mode turns on, stepped with the world
#          while it lasts, and freed when the mode turns off. the family's
#          step advances it where the set it steps holds it and passes it by
#          where it does not, so a run that shows neither pays for neither.
#          it is never saved, copied, journaled or written by an edit, since
#          the state gives it again
#
# the state and rule layers are a cell's word, its exact value: a value for
# each of them, in the set's order, each at its layer's width. a word is what
# a fresh cell of a state is written as (cellar.rule fresh), what a copy, a
# snapshot, the journal, a world file and a format that keeps exact values
# carry, and what an edit writes. it has no width of its own: a set holds as
# many rule layers as its owner needs, and a word holds that many values, one
# u32 each wherever it travels, so a run of n cells' words is n times the
# set's word length of values, a cell's values together. a format that
# carries states alone carries the state layer's, which the family reads a
# cell's state from. zero in every layer is the quiescent background: what a
# chunk that does not exist reads as and what a chunk just made holds.
#
# a cell is live when its state layer's value is, read through the family's
# sense, or when it holds a value but zero in a rule layer its family declares
# live: a field the step spreads whatever the state layer holds, as a second
# chemical's is. such a value also keeps its chunk warm, so a chunk is freed
# only once every live layer of every cell in it is zero. a rule layer not
# declared live is read by its family's step alone, so a family keeps its
# values where its state layer is live or warm, or lets them go with the chunk.
# a cell's state is likewise the family's to read from its whole word
# (cellar.rule word_state), its state layer's value and its rule layers'.
#
# a set is ordered. the state layer is layer 0, the rule layers follow in the
# order declared, and the view layers come last, so a view layer coming or
# going never moves a rule layer. a layer is named by its place in the set.
#
# a set's first view layer, where it has one, is its shown layer: the one the
# display channels are read from. a cell an edit writes starts its shown
# value over from its new state, as the layer started: the value a fresh live
# cell holds there where it is live, else zero. shared code reads a cell as its sensed value,
# its state layer's value with its shown layer's value above it, from the
# state layer's width up (sensed), and the family's sense reads what is live
# from that value, and what is warm, its heat and its age. a set's state and
# shown layers fit one word together. a set with no view layer is sensed by
# its state layer's value alone, so a family whose state layer holds its
# display channels keeps them there.
#
# a layer is addressed by layer, then slot, then cell. a slot's span of a
# layer is span_words(width) words of 32 bits, CELLS * width / 32 of them and
# at least 128, so no two slots share a word. cell i of a slot, row-major,
# lies in word cell_word(width, i) of the span at bit cell_shift(width, i):
# cells pack from the low bit, 32 / width of them to a word, and a word's
# cells lie in one row, so a step that works a word at a time steps 32 / width
# cells at once.
#
# where a span lies is the store's to say and no one else's. the host holds a
# layer as one array of every slot's span in slot order (span_at). the GPU
# holds each layer's two cells in shards, buffers each holding a run of slots'
# spans, and names a slot's shard and the word its span starts at there
# (span), from the slot alone (cellar.layout shard_of), so a span never
# straddles two shards and a pool grows without moving one.
#
# the stages reach every layer by device address through the shard table the
# meta head names (cellar.layout.Shards), so a stage binds no layer and a set
# holds as many as LAYERS_MAX whatever the device binds. the meta head names
# the set's layers and their widths (cellar.layout SET_AT and WIDTHS_AT,
# set_word and widths_add): the shared stages read the state layer at its
# width, the stages that judge a cell live, the census, the mark and the
# reduce, read every live rule layer too, and the census, the reduce and the
# draw read a cell's sensed value through the shown layer. a layer's cells c,
# 0 or 1, hold the generation a step of serial s left where c is s's low bit,
# so a stage finds the front from the serial it reads.

use cellar.layout;

# the widest layer, and the bits an exact value holds
pub val WIDTH_MAX: u32 = 32;
# the most layers a set holds, of every role
pub val LAYERS_MAX: u32 = 8;

$if (LAYERS_MAX != layout.SHARD_LAYERS) {
    $error("the shard table names another number of layers than a set holds");
}

# the roles a layer can have
pub val STATE: u32 = 0;
pub val RULE:  u32 = 1;
pub val VIEW:  u32 = 2;

# 1 when width is one a layer may have, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 or 32, else 0
pub fun valid(width: u32) u32 {
    if (width == 1 || width == 2 || width == 4 || width == 8 || width == 16 || width == 32) { ret 1; }
    ret 0;
}

# the values a layer of a width can hold, as a mask of its low bits
#[inline]
pub fun mask(width: u32) u32 {
    if (width >= WIDTH_MAX) { ret 0xffffffff; }
    ret (1 << width) - 1;
}

# words of a slot's span of a layer of a width
#[inline]
pub fun span_words(width: u32) u32 {
    ret layout.CELLS * width / WIDTH_MAX;
}

# the width whose slot's span is words long, for a stage that sees a span
# only as words
pub fun width_of(words: u32) u32 {
    ret words * WIDTH_MAX / layout.CELLS;
}

# the first word of a slot's span in a layer held as one buffer, slot by slot
#[inline]
pub fun span_at(width: u32, slot: u32) u32 {
    ret slot * span_words(width);
}

# the word of a slot's span holding cell i
#[inline]
pub fun cell_word(width: u32, i: u32) u32 {
    if (width == WIDTH_MAX) { ret i; }
    ret (i * width) / WIDTH_MAX;
}

# the bit of its word where cell i's value starts
#[inline]
pub fun cell_shift(width: u32, i: u32) u32 {
    if (width == WIDTH_MAX) { ret 0; }
    ret (i * width) % WIDTH_MAX;
}

# the word of a layer held as one buffer holding cell i of a slot
#[inline]
pub fun cell_at(width: u32, slot: u32, i: u32) u32 {
    ret span_at(width, slot) + cell_word(width, i);
}

# where a slot's span of layer k's cells c, 0 or 1, at a width lies in the
# shards the table sh names, the slot found by cellar.layout where under the
# pool's geometry (cellar.layout SHARD_AT)
#[inline]
pub fun span(sh: *layout.Shards, k: u32, c: u32, at: layout.Where, width: u32) layout.Span {
    ret layout.Span{p: sh.v[layout.cells_entry(k, c, at.shard)], at: at.index * span_words(width)};
}

# cells a word holds
pub fun per_word(width: u32) u32 {
    ret WIDTH_MAX / width;
}

# cell i's value in the word holding it
#[inline]
pub fun read(w: u32, width: u32, i: u32) u32 {
    if (width == WIDTH_MAX) { ret w; }
    ret (w >> cell_shift(width, i)) & mask(width);
}

# cell i's value v placed in an otherwise empty word, for a step that builds
# its words a cell at a time (ends)
#[inline]
pub fun place(width: u32, i: u32, v: u32) u32 {
    if (width == WIDTH_MAX) { ret v; }
    ret (v & mask(width)) << cell_shift(width, i);
}

# the word holding cell i with its value replaced by v
#[inline]
pub fun write(w: u32, width: u32, i: u32, v: u32) u32 {
    val m: u32 = mask(width) << cell_shift(width, i);
    ret (w & ~m) | ((v << cell_shift(width, i)) & m);
}

# 1 when cell i is the last its word holds, so a word built a cell at a time
# is complete once it is placed, else 0
#[inline]
pub fun ends(width: u32, i: u32) u32 {
    if (width == WIDTH_MAX)                 { ret 1; }
    if (((i + 1) * width) % WIDTH_MAX == 0) { ret 1; }
    ret 0;
}

# the meta head's widths word (cellar.layout.WIDTHS_AT) with layer k's width
# added, four bits a layer from the low bits: the width's log2 plus one, so 0
# names no layer
pub fun widths_add(code: u32, k: u32, width: u32) u32 {
    var c: u32 = 1;
    for ((1 << (c - 1)) < width) { c = c + 1; }
    ret code | (c << (k * 4));
}

# the width of layer k a widths word names, 0 for none
#[inline]
pub fun width_in(code: u32, k: u32) u32 {
    val c: u32 = (code >> (k * 4)) & 0xf;
    if (c == 0) { ret 0; }
    ret 1 << (c - 1);
}

# the meta head's set word (cellar.layout.SET_AT): the set's n layers in the
# low four bits, its shown layer above them, 0 for none since the state layer
# is never shown, and a bit per live rule layer from SET_LIVE, by layer
pub fun set_word(n: u32, shown: u32, lives: u32) u32 {
    ret n | (shown << 4) | (lives << SET_LIVE);
}

# where the set word's live bits start
pub val SET_LIVE: u32 = 8;

# the layers a set word names
#[inline]
pub fun set_layers(w: u32) u32 {
    ret w & 0xf;
}

# the shown layer a set word names, 0 for none
#[inline]
pub fun set_shown(w: u32) u32 {
    ret (w >> 4) & 0xf;
}

# the live rule layers a set word names, a bit a layer by its place in the set
#[inline]
pub fun set_lives(w: u32) u32 {
    ret w >> SET_LIVE;
}

# a cell's sensed value: its state layer's value v, with its shown layer's
# value h above it from bit width, the state layer's width, up. width is the
# word's whole width where the set has no shown layer, and h is then ignored
#[inline]
pub fun sensed(v: u32, h: u32, width: u32) u32 {
    if (width >= WIDTH_MAX) { ret v; }
    ret v | (h << width);
}

test address__packs_every_width_low_bit_first_a_row_to_a_word {
    var width: u32 = 1;
    for (width <= WIDTH_MAX) {
        if (valid(width) == 0)                                     { ret 1; }
        if (span_words(width) * WIDTH_MAX != layout.CELLS * width) { ret 2; }
        # a slot's span ends where the next one's begins
        if (span_at(width, 3) + span_words(width) != span_at(width, 4)) { ret 3; }
        if (width_of(span_words(width)) != width)                       { ret 3; }
        var i: u32 = 0;
        for (i < layout.CELLS) {
            # a word's cells lie in one row
            val first: u32 = cell_word(width, i) * per_word(width);
            if (first / layout.SIDE != i / layout.SIDE)      { ret 4; }
            if (cell_shift(width, i) != (i - first) * width) { ret 5; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        # writing a cell leaves its neighbours in the word alone
        val all: u32 = 0xa5a5a5a5;
        val v:   u32 = 0x5a5a5a5a & mask(width);
        val j:   u32 = per_word(width) - 1;
        val put: u32 = write(all, width, j, v);
        if (read(put, width, j) != v)                                                                         { ret 6; }
        if ((put & ~(mask(width) << cell_shift(width, j))) != (all & ~(mask(width) << cell_shift(width, j)))) { ret 7; }
        if (place(width, j, v) != (v << cell_shift(width, j)))                                                { ret 8; }
        if (ends(width, j) != 1 || (width < WIDTH_MAX && ends(width, 0) != 0))                                { ret 9; }
        width = width * 2;
    }
    if (valid(0) != 0 || valid(3) != 0 || valid(64) != 0) { ret 10; }
    # a widths word names each layer's width, and nothing past them
    val code: u32 = widths_add(widths_add(0, 0, 16), 1, 1);
    if (width_in(code, 0) != 16 || width_in(code, 1) != 1 || width_in(code, 2) != 0) { ret 15; }
    if (width_in(widths_add(0, LAYERS_MAX - 1, 32), LAYERS_MAX - 1) != 32)           { ret 16; }
    # a set word names its layers, its shown layer and its live ones
    val sw: u32 = set_word(4, 3, 0x6);
    if (set_layers(sw) != 4 || set_shown(sw) != 3 || set_lives(sw) != 0x6 || set_shown(set_word(1, 0, 0)) != 0) { ret 17; }
    if (sensed(1, 0x1ff, 1) != 0x3ff || sensed(0xabc, 7, WIDTH_MAX) != 0xabc)                                   { ret 18; }
    ret 0;
}
